{{!-- The item controls, one cluster in one order on every row that lists a carried thing: the ten
      numbered lines, the Petty and Belongings list, and an NPC's Items tab. It was written three
      times and had drifted — the Petty tab had no Post, the NPC row led with Set Aside — so an item
      behaved differently depending on where it was listed.

      The order: roll, the two "read it aloud" gestures, the two that say where the thing is, then
      the three that address the item itself. A control that writes the document is drawn only when
      the sheet is `editable`; one that reads, opens or posts is drawn for anyone who can see the
      sheet. Core disables every `<button>` on a sheet the user cannot write, but an `<a data-action>`
      is not a form element and stays live — it would reach an update and a permission toast.

      @param item      the row's item view (`actor-sheet.js#itemView`)
      @param editable  @root.editable — whether the write controls are drawn at all --}}
<span class="cairn-item-controls">
    {{#if item.system.equipped}}{{#if item.system.damage}}
    <a data-action="rollDamage" data-tooltip="{{localize 'CAIRN.RollDamageHint'}}"><i class="fas fa-dice-d20"></i></a>
    {{/if}}{{/if}}

    {{#if editable}}
    {{!-- Cast only shows on an EQUIPPED Spellbook: a spell is cast by holding the book in both
          hands and reading it aloud, so a book not in hand cannot be read. Consume stands beside
          it — "They disappear after one use" (`core-rules.md` → Scrolls). A scroll is petty by
          rule, so it is never on the ten and this control is never drawn there. --}}
    {{#if item.canCast}}
    <a data-action="spellCast" data-tooltip="{{localize 'CAIRN.CastSpell'}}"><i class="fas fa-wand-sparkles"></i></a>
    {{/if}}
    {{#if item.canConsume}}
    <a data-action="itemConsume" data-tooltip="{{localize 'CAIRN.ConsumeScroll'}}"><i class="fas fa-wand-sparkles"></i></a>
    {{/if}}

    {{!-- Equipped is a CLOSED FIST at full ink; unequipped is an OPEN HAND, outlined and soft. It
          was one glyph in two shades before, and at 18px the difference between them was not a
          difference anyone could see. Both glyphs sit in the same 18px cell, so toggling one moves
          nothing else in the row. A zero-slot thing can still be a weapon or a spellbook — the
          model says so (`documents/item.js#isEquipable`) — and a thing not under direct
          possession is not equipable, which is the model's answer already. --}}
    {{#if item.system.isEquipable}}
    <a data-action="itemEquipToggle" class="cairn-equip{{#if item.system.equipped}} equipped{{/if}}"
        data-tooltip="{{#if item.system.equipped}}{{localize 'CAIRN.ItemUnequip'}}{{else}}{{localize 'CAIRN.ItemEquip'}}{{/if}}">
        <i class="{{#if item.system.equipped}}fas fa-hand-fist{{else}}far fa-hand{{/if}}"></i>
    </a>
    {{/if}}

    {{!-- Set aside, or taken back: a figure that walks with you, or the camp you left it at — two
          outlines, not two shades. On the ten the thing is always carried, so only the walking
          figure is ever drawn there. A Fatigue never carries it: "a character forced to add
          Fatigue with no free slots must drop an item" (`core-rules.md`), and the escape from that
          is dropping the item, never the Fatigue. --}}
    {{#if item.system.isStashable}}
    <a data-action="setAsideToggle" class="cairn-carried{{#if item.system.carried}} is-on{{/if}}"
        data-tooltip="{{#if item.system.carried}}{{localize 'CAIRN.SetAside'}}{{else}}{{localize 'CAIRN.TakeBack'}}{{/if}}">
        <i class="fas {{#if item.system.carried}}fa-person-walking{{else}}fa-campground{{/if}}"></i>
    </a>
    {{/if}}
    {{/if}}

    {{!-- A Fatigue carries none of the three: its circle in the track beside the ten is the only
          thing that puts one there and the only thing that takes it away. --}}
    {{#unless item.isFatigue}}
    <a data-action="itemEdit" data-tooltip="{{localize 'CAIRN.EditItem'}}"><i class="fas fa-pencil"></i></a>
    {{!-- The description, read out loud, between the pencil and the cross. An item with nothing
          written keeps the glyph and loses the action, so the row is the same shape on every line
          and the answer to "why can I not click this" is visible rather than absent. --}}
    {{#if item.hasDescription}}
    <a data-action="itemPost" data-tooltip="{{localize 'CAIRN.PostToChat'}}"><i class="fas fa-scroll"></i></a>
    {{else}}
    <a class="is-disabled" aria-disabled="true" data-tooltip="{{localize 'CAIRN.PostToChat'}}"><i class="fas fa-scroll"></i></a>
    {{/if}}
    {{#if editable}}
    <a data-action="itemDelete" data-tooltip="{{localize 'CAIRN.DeleteItem'}}"><i class="fas fa-xmark"></i></a>
    {{/if}}
    {{/unless}}
</span>
